# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Course material
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The step-by-step lessons live alongside this repository but are deliberately
# not part of it. The repository is the engineering project; the course is the
# instructor's material.
learning/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# scripts/build.sh assembles the deployable site here. It is derived from the
# tracked source files, so it is never committed.
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider plugins and module caches — re-downloaded by `terraform init`.
.terraform/
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# State contains resource attributes and can contain secrets. Never commit it.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup

# Real variable values, including account-specific names and domains.
# terraform.tfvars.example IS tracked and shows the expected shape.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# Saved plans are binary and can leak values.
*.tfplan
plan.out

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is intentionally NOT ignored. It pins provider
# versions and hashes so CI and every engineer resolve identical providers.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials — belt and braces. Nothing here should ever exist in the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials
aws-credentials*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
